    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. **BUILD SUCCESS** with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a human-readable `telephoneDisplay` field while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164. All three owner response paths (GET, POST-created, PUT-updated) flow through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so a single mapper change covers them.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Telephones.java`** \u2014 new `toDisplay(String)` helper. It normalizes the input via the existing `toE164`, splits off a recognized country code, and groups the national digits into space-separated runs of three (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). Returns `null` for numbers that can't form valid E.164. Unknown country codes fall back to grouping all post-`+` digits in threes.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` computed from `owner.getTelephone()` via `Telephones.toDisplay(...)`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe acceptance test's exact expectations are met: POSTing `\"0412 345 678\"` yields `$.telephone == \"+61412345678\"` and `$.telephoneDisplay == \"+61 412 345 678\"`.",
